  "note": "Annual election of the Newtownards Urban Council, January 1926. The local weekly reports that there was no election, the retiring members being returned unopposed; the paper names the five members but does not print a ward-by-ward list, so they are recorded together for the borough. The report reads: 'There will be no election, there being no opposition to the retiring members, who have been accordingly declared elected. The retiring members were Messrs. T. R. Lavery, J.P., M.P.; R. J. Beckett, Robert Edgar, Robert George, and David Johnston.' No wards are printed with the names. Returned unopposed."
